{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "Sharing the Housework"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Recycle, Recycle, Recycle!"}, {"type": "position", "content": 10}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 7}, {"type": "level", "content": "B2.1"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Identify and describe issues  in written and spoken situations according to social contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": " Integrates a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge when dealing with problems and difficulties. "}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": " Integrates a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge when dealing with problems and difficulties. "}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": " Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear"}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": " Integrates a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge when dealing with problems and difficulties. "}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": " Integrates a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge when dealing with problems and difficulties. "}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": " Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. "}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": " Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. "}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": " Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. "}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "The Position of <span class=\"italic\">Not</span>"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "When you want to emphasize that something or an action is opposite to what is expected, use <span class=\"italic\">not</span>, rather than a contraction in the sentence."}, {"type": "text", "content": "For example:<br/><span class=\"italic\">Otherwise things will <span class=\"strong\">not</span> change, will they?</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "The <span class=\"strong\">not</span> shows a firmness on the part of the speaker while still being polite."}, {"type": "text", "content": "When speaking, the <span class=\"strong\">not</span> is pronounced louder and longer than it is normally. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Is that not what we all want?"}, {"type": "example", "content": "We should remind other people not to litter too."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Is that not what scientists are saying?"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Obviously we have not been doing what we were supposed to be doing."}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " Explaining How Things Were Done"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "  You use <span class=\"italic\">be supposed to</span> and <span class=\"italic\">was going</span> to to explain how things were done."}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use the structure <span class=\"strong\">be supposed to </span>when you want to talk about expectations, obligations or arrangements. You can use this structure using the Past tense to talk about things that you were obligated to do, but didn't or couldn't do. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "The structure is: <br /><br /> Subject + To be +<span class=\"italic\"> supposed to</span> + verb <br /><br /> <span class=\"italic\">Another thing <span class=\"strong\">we were all supposed to be doing</span> to help the environment was not litter. </span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "**Pronunciation tip**:<br /> When you say be supposed to, you link the /d/ and /t/ sounds together.  <br /><br /> Like this: Be suppose_to"}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use the structure<span class=\"strong\"> was going to </span> when you want to talk about things that you had planned or intended to do."}, {"type": "text", "content": "The structure is:<br /><br />  <span class=\"italic\">was</span>/<span class=\"italic\">were </span>+ <span class=\"italic\">going to</span> + verb <br /><br />  <span class=\"italic\">You <span class=\"strong\">were going to spend</span> less time driving and more time walking. </span>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "We were supposed to recycle. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "You were supposed to take all of your recyclables out of the weekly trash, too! "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Obviously we have not been doing what we were supposed to be doing or there wouldn't be a crisis!"}, {"type": "example", "content": "You were going to spend less time driving and more time walking."}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn9le07ob10re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to recycle"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to treat or process to reuse "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:  We were supposed to recycle."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le07ob10aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " These are words you use to talk about saving the environment."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "environment "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the aggregate of surrounding things, conditions, or influences"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: There has never been a better time to start caring for the environment, has there?"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le07ob10aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "washable "}, {"type": "definition", "content": " that can be washed"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:  When you wipe up the kitchen, use a washable cloth instead of paper towels."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le07ob10aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "tip"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a small piece of advice  "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: She gave me tip on recycling."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le07ob10aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "recyclables "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "things that can be used again "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:You were supposed to take all of your recyclables out of the weekly trash, too! "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le07ob10aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "litter "}, {"type": "definition", "content": " trash,garbage  "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:Unfortunately, litter has been piling up in our cities and natural areas. We should remind other people not to litter too. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le07ob10aud06"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Choose two things you want to make posters for addressing pollution problems (water pollution, litter, recycling, exhaust pollution \u2026)"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Make up two separate posters linking domestic activities to the pollution problems."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Explain how to change things."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Use questions asking for clarification on the poster."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Bring your posters to class and put them up with other posters."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Read posters that other students have created."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I create two posters dealing with pollution linked with domestic activities."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I  explain how to change things, using : be supposed to, was/were supposed to, and was/were going to."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I use questions for clarification with not."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I put my posters up in the class and I read other posters."}]}], "labs": [{"exercises": [{"template_override": 1, "stimuli_ids": [0], "type": "WLC", "questions": [], "img_path": "", "id": 0, "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can talk about domestic activities."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can explain how to do things. "}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can ask for clarification. "}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": " What pollution problems need to be addressed in your country?"}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": " How important is recycling to you, your community and your country?"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Welcome"}]}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "You have 2 tries"}, {"type": "text", "content": "you have 1 attempt left"}], "correct_feedback": "Correct", "allowed_attempts": 2, "incorrect_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "try again"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Maybe next time"}]}}, {"type": "free_header_t